**Line items with no value available in the filing set** (Retail health GWP, IFRS PAT, Claims ratio [IGAAP/IFRS], Expense ratio, Commission ratio, Combined ratio, Solvency ratio, Retail health market share, AUM) have been omitted from the table above per the filtering rule — none were disclosed anywhere across the five specified documents.

## Key Observations

- **PAT of ₹7.44 crore** for 9MFY25 is markedly low relative to standalone Q2 (₹13.02 cr) and Q3 (₹13.24 cr) FY25 figures reported elsewhere in the same filing. The filing's **Note 5** explains this: an excess Expense of Management (EoM) of **₹198.37 crore** was transferred from the revenue account to the P&L account for the nine-month period under a regulatory forbearance adjustment, which suppressed the cumulative YTD bottom line.
- **Two EoM ratio bases** appear in the filing: **51.31%** (EoM as a percentage of Net Written Premium, per the Regulation 52(4) analytical ratios table) versus **39%** (per Note 5, computed on a gross direct premium basis). The 51.31% figure is reported above as it aligns with the standard NWP-basis convention requested.
- **NEP of ₹3,367.04 crore** was derived by aggregating the three active segments disclosed in Annexure II (Health, Personal Accident, Travel) — Fire, Marine, Motor, Crop, and Miscellaneous segments were all nil, consistent with Niva Bupa's business as a pure health/PA/travel insurer.
- **Solvency ratio** is referenced qualitatively in Note 10 (regarding a methodology change) but no numeric value is disclosed in this filing's extracted text.
- **A dual yield figure** is disclosed: **5.27%** (without unrealized gains) and **6.09%** (with unrealized gains) — the without-unrealized-gains figure (5.27%) is reported above as the more conservative, commonly-cited convention.

## Suggested Next Steps

To fill the remaining blanks (Retail health GWP, Claims/Expense/Commission/Combined ratios, Solvency ratio value, Retail health market share, AUM, IFRS PAT), you would need:
1. Niva Bupa's **"Investor Presentation — 9MFY25"** deck (typically published alongside results but not included among the five source documents here).
2. The **IRDAI NL-1 (Revenue Account) and NL-2 (Expenses Schedule)** quarterly public disclosure PDFs, and the **Balance Sheet return**, for the December 31, 2024 quarter — these are filed separately from the SEBI Regulation 33/52 results PDF and were not part of the five documents provided.</ans>
